This project is a RISC-V operating system running on QEMU with the host machine being Ubuntu 20.04. 
The project contains approximately 27,000 lines of code (including test code) and features 70 system call APIs, which include:
Memory Management: Virtual memory, buddy slab memory allocation, shared memory, page swapping.
Multiprocessor Process Scheduling: Process management, round-robin scheduling, CFS scheduling, CPU load balancing.
Synchronization Mechanisms: Semaphores, events, message queues, signals, pipes.
File System: Virtual File System (VFS), logging system.
Network Stack: ARP, ICMP, IP, UDP, TCP, DNS, and socket interface.
This project has drawn inspiration from several open-source operating system projects and received assistance from ChatGPT. 
Many of the code components are not original and are intended purely for the purpose of learning operating system concepts.

The project configuration is based on the XV6 project configuration. For host machine configuration, please refer to XV6. Additionally, 
before running the project, ensure that the host machine has an ens33 network interface. If not, please add a network interface with that name. 
Detailed configuration can be found in the Makefile located in the root directory. To run the project, use the command make qemu.

